<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    "Add a place": the sub-screen reached from "+ ADD PLACE" in the Places tab's saved-places heading.

    **What the screen is for.** Saving the vet, groomer, park or shop the user is *standing in*. The
    device's GPS gives the position a starting point — the screen asks for a fix the moment it opens, so
    by the time the name has been typed it is usually already in — which is what reduces the common case
    to "type the name, press save". The map underneath is then draggable, so a fix that landed on the
    wrong side of the road, or a place the user is not standing in at all, can be corrected by moving the
    pin; see MapEmbedView for how a coordinate is read out of a map the app cannot ask.

    Top to bottom:
      - **The shared header** (monogram, "Add place", theme toggle, pet count), fixed above the page as
        on the tabs. It is what keeps this screen recognisably part of the Places tab while the bottom
        bar keeps that tab lit.
      - Everything else scrolls as one page:
          · the **heading block** — a round back button beside "Add a place" and the sentence naming
            the moment the screen is for;
          · the **live map** — a real Google map at the current fix, with a status chip in its corner,
            or a placeholder saying what is being waited for;
          · the **current-location card** — the fix in words and figures, and the buttons that take
            another one or fall back to the demo position;
          · the **save fields** — name, category, note;
          · the **summary** of what will be saved, then "SAVE PLACE".

    **Why the map and its placeholder are both declared here and toggled,** rather than one view that
    draws whichever it needs: they are genuinely different things — a WebView showing Google's tiles,
    and a centred column of app views — and a single custom view would have to be both. Two siblings
    whose visibility follows one piece of state is the plainest way to say "one or the other".

    **Why one NestedScrollView** rather than a RecyclerView for the page: the same reasoning as
    fragment_places.xml. These are a handful of stateful views, not rows.

    **Why a CoordinatorLayout at the root:** so Snackbars attach here and appear above the floating
    bottom navigation bar rather than underneath it — see fragment_places.xml.
-->
<androidx.coordinatorlayout.widget.CoordinatorLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:app="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent"
    tools:context=".ui.place.AddPlaceFragment">

    <!-- The header takes the height it needs; the page takes the rest through height 0 + weight 1. -->
    <LinearLayout
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="match_parent"
        android:orientation="vertical">

        <!-- The shared header, as a nested binding (`binding.header`). -->
        <include
            android:id="@+id/header"
            layout="@layout/view_tab_header" />

        <androidx.core.widget.NestedScrollView
            android:id="@+id/addPlaceScroll"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="0dp"
            android:layout_weight="1"
            android:clipToPadding="false"
            android:paddingBottom="@dimen/add_place_scroll_padding_bottom">

            <LinearLayout
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:orientation="vertical"
                android:paddingStart="@dimen/screen_padding"
                android:paddingEnd="@dimen/screen_padding">

                <!-- ============================== Heading ==============================
                     The round back button and the text block beside it. gravity top rather than
                     centre, so the button lines up with the *first* line of a heading that wraps
                     rather than drifting down beside a two-line block. -->
                <LinearLayout
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/spacing_xs"
                    android:baselineAligned="false"
                    android:gravity="top"
                    android:orientation="horizontal">

                    <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
                        android:id="@+id/backButton"
                        style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.BackButton"
                        android:contentDescription="@string/cd_add_place_back" />

                    <LinearLayout
                        android:layout_width="0dp"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/spacing_md"
                        android:layout_weight="1"
                        android:orientation="vertical">

                        <!-- accessibilityHeading marks this as the page's heading, so TalkBack users
                             can jump straight to it with heading navigation. -->
                        <TextView
                            style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.Title"
                            android:layout_width="match_parent"
                            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                            android:accessibilityHeading="true"
                            android:text="@string/add_place_heading"
                            tools:targetApi="p" />

                        <!-- The moment the screen is for, in one line. -->
                        <TextView
                            style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.Subtitle"
                            android:layout_width="match_parent"
                            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                            android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/add_place_subtitle_gap"
                            android:text="@string/add_place_subheading" />

                    </LinearLayout>

                </LinearLayout>

                <!-- ============================= The live map =============================
                     A real Google map centred on the current fix — see MapEmbedView for why it is a
                     WebView over the keyless embed URL, and how its tiles are tinted for the app's
                     theme. The card's own background is the map's loading ground; see the matching
                     card in fragment_places.xml. -->
                <com.google.android.material.card.MaterialCardView
                    android:id="@+id/gpsMapCard"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="@dimen/gps_map_height"
                    android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/spacing_md"
                    app:cardBackgroundColor="?attr/colorMapGround"
                    app:cardElevation="@dimen/card_elevation"
                    app:shapeAppearanceOverlay="@style/ShapeAppearance.PetCare.XLarge">

                    <FrameLayout
                        android:layout_width="match_parent"
                        android:layout_height="match_parent">

                        <!-- Shown only once there is a fix: a map of nowhere in particular would be
                             worse than saying what is being waited for. -->
                        <com.prash.petcare.ui.place.MapEmbedView
                            android:id="@+id/gpsMap"
                            android:layout_width="match_parent"
                            android:layout_height="match_parent"
                            android:contentDescription="@string/cd_add_place_map"
                            android:visibility="gone"
                            tools:visibility="visible" />

                        <!-- The placeholder in the map's place: the "you are here" dot in its tinted
                             well over a line of explanation. The same dot as the card below, so the
                             two read as one status rather than two.

                             Hidden from TalkBack because the card underneath states the same thing in
                             full — a screen reader would otherwise hear it twice. -->
                        <LinearLayout
                            android:id="@+id/mapPlaceholder"
                            android:layout_width="match_parent"
                            android:layout_height="match_parent"
                            android:gravity="center"
                            android:importantForAccessibility="no"
                            android:orientation="vertical"
                            android:paddingStart="@dimen/spacing_lg"
                            android:paddingEnd="@dimen/spacing_lg">

                            <!-- A FrameLayout because the dot is genuinely *centred on* the well
                                 rather than beside it. -->
                            <FrameLayout
                                android:layout_width="@dimen/gps_map_placeholder_well_size"
                                android:layout_height="@dimen/gps_map_placeholder_well_size"
                                android:background="@drawable/bg_gps_dot_well">

                                <View
                                    android:layout_width="@dimen/gps_map_placeholder_dot_size"
                                    android:layout_height="@dimen/gps_map_placeholder_dot_size"
                                    android:layout_gravity="center"
                                    android:background="@drawable/bg_gps_dot" />

                            </FrameLayout>

                            <TextView
                                android:id="@+id/mapPlaceholderText"
                                style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.MapPlaceholder"
                                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                                android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/spacing_md"
                                tools:text="Finding your position…" />

                        </LinearLayout>

                        <!-- The layer toggle, in the corner opposite the status chip. Shown only
                             alongside a real map — see AddPlaceFragment.renderMap: there is no layer
                             to choose when there are no tiles. -->
                        <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
                            android:id="@+id/mapLayerButton"
                            style="@style/PetCare.Map.LayerToggle"
                            android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                            android:layout_gravity="top|end"
                            android:layout_margin="@dimen/gps_map_chip_inset"
                            android:visibility="gone"
                            tools:text="@string/map_layer_switch_to_satellite"
                            tools:visibility="visible" />

                        <!--
                            The pin that hangs over the middle of the map while it is being dragged.

                            **Why it is only visible during a drag** (AddPlaceFragment toggles it):
                            at rest, Google's own pin inside the embed already marks the centre, and a
                            second marker sitting on top of it would read as two different answers to
                            "where is this place?". While the map is moving that pin slides away with
                            the tiles, and this one is what shows the point being aimed at.

                            **Why it is translated upwards by half its height.** The coordinate the
                            screen saves is the centre of the map — the middle of this FrameLayout — and
                            a pin's *tip* is what marks a point, not the middle of its balloon. Shifting
                            the whole drawable up by half its own height puts the tip on the centre. See
                            ic_map_pin.xml.
                        -->
                        <ImageView
                            android:id="@+id/mapCentrePin"
                            android:layout_width="@dimen/map_centre_pin_size"
                            android:layout_height="@dimen/map_centre_pin_size"
                            android:layout_gravity="center"
                            android:importantForAccessibility="no"
                            android:src="@drawable/ic_map_pin"
                            android:translationY="@dimen/map_centre_pin_offset"
                            android:visibility="gone"
                            tools:visibility="visible" />

                        <!-- The status chip over the map's top-left corner: a coloured dot and a
                             label. Laid over *both* the map and the placeholder, because it answers
                             the same question in either case. -->
                        <LinearLayout
                            android:id="@+id/gpsStatusChip"
                            style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.GpsChip"
                            android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                            android:layout_gravity="top|start"
                            android:layout_margin="@dimen/gps_map_chip_inset"
                            android:orientation="horizontal">

                            <!-- Tinted from code, because the colour *is* the status — see
                                 AddPlaceFragment.renderMap. -->
                            <View
                                android:id="@+id/gpsStatusDot"
                                android:layout_width="@dimen/gps_map_chip_dot_size"
                                android:layout_height="@dimen/gps_map_chip_dot_size"
                                android:background="@drawable/bg_status_dot" />

                            <TextView
                                android:id="@+id/gpsStatusChipLabel"
                                style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.GpsChipLabel"
                                android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                                android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/spacing_xs"
                                tools:text="Live GPS" />

                        </LinearLayout>

                    </FrameLayout>

                </com.google.android.material.card.MaterialCardView>

                <!-- The one line that says the map is a control rather than a picture. It has to be
                     said: a draggable map looks exactly like an undraggable one, and without this the
                     only position most users would ever save is the one the GPS handed them. Hidden
                     along with the map whenever there is no position to drag — see
                     AddPlaceFragment.renderMap. -->
                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/mapDragHintText"
                    style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.MapHint"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/spacing_sm"
                    android:text="@string/add_place_map_drag_hint" />

                <!-- ======================== The current-location card ========================
                     The fix in words and figures, and the two ways of changing it.

                     A dark card in both themes: it is a single strong statement — "this is where you
                     are" — and a white card would make it one more field in the form. -->
                <com.google.android.material.card.MaterialCardView
                    android:id="@+id/gpsCard"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/spacing_md"
                    app:cardBackgroundColor="@color/gps_card_ground"
                    app:cardCornerRadius="@dimen/gps_card_corner_radius"
                    app:cardElevation="0dp">

                    <LinearLayout
                        android:layout_width="match_parent"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:orientation="vertical"
                        android:padding="@dimen/gps_card_padding">

                        <!-- The status dot and the three lines of text beside it. -->
                        <LinearLayout
                            android:layout_width="match_parent"
                            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                            android:baselineAligned="false"
                            android:gravity="center_vertical"
                            android:orientation="horizontal">

                            <FrameLayout
                                android:layout_width="@dimen/gps_card_dot_well_size"
                                android:layout_height="@dimen/gps_card_dot_well_size"
                                android:background="@drawable/bg_gps_dot_well">

                                <!-- Tinted from code like the chip's dot, and for the same reason. -->
                                <View
                                    android:id="@+id/gpsCardDot"
                                    android:layout_width="@dimen/gps_card_dot_size"
                                    android:layout_height="@dimen/gps_card_dot_size"
                                    android:layout_gravity="center"
                                    android:background="@drawable/bg_gps_dot" />

                            </FrameLayout>

                            <LinearLayout
                                android:layout_width="0dp"
                                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                                android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/spacing_md"
                                android:layout_weight="1"
                                android:orientation="vertical">

                                <!-- "CURRENT LOCATION", or "CHOSEN LOCATION" once the pin has been
                                     dragged: the card stops describing the phone at that point, and a
                                     label that went on claiming otherwise would be the one line on the
                                     screen that was wrong. Set from AddPlaceFragment.renderGpsCard. -->
                                <TextView
                                    android:id="@+id/hereLabelText"
                                    style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.HereLabel"
                                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                                    tools:text="@string/add_place_here_label" />

                                <!-- "You are here", "Finding your position…", "Location unavailable". -->
                                <TextView
                                    android:id="@+id/hereTitleText"
                                    style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.HereArea"
                                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                                    android:layout_marginTop="2dp"
                                    tools:text="You are here" />

                                <!-- The coordinates, the device's own accuracy estimate and the
                                     distance from home — or, when there is no fix, why not. The
                                     accuracy is shown rather than hidden: it is what lets somebody
                                     decide whether to save this fix or step outside first. -->
                                <TextView
                                    android:id="@+id/hereMetaText"
                                    style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.HereCoordinates"
                                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                                    android:layout_marginTop="3dp"
                                    tools:text="27.6743° N, 85.3094° E · ±8 m · 0.1 km from home" />

                            </LinearLayout>

                        </LinearLayout>

                        <!-- The buttons.

                             "Refresh location" is sized to its own label, as the design draws it. The
                             demo pill — which only appears when location is denied or unsupported —
                             takes whatever width is left (weight 1 on a zero width) rather than its
                             own content width, so the pair can never be wider than the card: on a
                             narrow phone at a large font size two content-sized pills would overflow,
                             and the one that fell off the edge would be the way *out* of the refused
                             permission. -->
                        <LinearLayout
                            android:layout_width="match_parent"
                            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                            android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/spacing_md"
                            android:baselineAligned="false"
                            android:orientation="horizontal">

                            <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
                                android:id="@+id/refreshLocationButton"
                                style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.GpsButton.Outline"
                                android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                                tools:text="@string/add_place_gps_refresh" />

                            <!-- Only when location is denied or unsupported: the way to walk through
                                 the rest of the screen anyway. -->
                            <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
                                android:id="@+id/useDemoLocationButton"
                                style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.GpsButton.Demo"
                                android:layout_width="0dp"
                                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                                android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/spacing_sm"
                                android:layout_weight="1"
                                android:text="@string/add_place_gps_use_demo"
                                android:visibility="gone"
                                tools:visibility="visible" />

                        </LinearLayout>

                    </LinearLayout>

                </com.google.android.material.card.MaterialCardView>

                <!-- ============================ The save fields ============================ -->

                <TextView
                    style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.FieldLabel"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:text="@string/add_place_name_label" />

                <com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputLayout
                    style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.Field"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content">

                    <!-- capWords because a place name is a proper noun. -->
                    <com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputEditText
                        android:id="@+id/nameInput"
                        style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.NameInput"
                        android:layout_width="match_parent"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:hint="@string/add_place_name_hint"
                        android:imeOptions="actionNext"
                        android:inputType="textCapWords" />

                </com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputLayout>

                <TextView
                    style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.FieldLabel"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:text="@string/add_place_category_label" />

                <!-- Vet · Grooming · Park · Store. The Tasks tab's filter chips, built in code from
                     PlaceCategory — see ui/common/FilterChips.kt — so the chosen pill gets exactly the
                     treatment every other chosen thing in the app does. A wrapping ChipGroup rather
                     than a scrolling row: four short pills fit two-and-two on the narrowest phone, and
                     a category hidden off the edge of a scroller is one that never gets chosen. -->
                <com.google.android.material.chip.ChipGroup
                    android:id="@+id/categoryChipGroup"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    app:chipSpacingHorizontal="@dimen/spacing_sm"
                    app:selectionRequired="true"
                    app:singleSelection="true" />

                <TextView
                    style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.FieldLabel"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:text="@string/add_place_note_label" />

                <com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputLayout
                    style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.Field"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content">

                    <!-- imeOptions actionDone, since this is the last field on the form. -->
                    <com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputEditText
                        android:id="@+id/noteInput"
                        style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.NoteInput"
                        android:layout_width="match_parent"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:hint="@string/add_place_note_hint"
                        android:imeOptions="actionDone"
                        android:inputType="textCapSentences" />

                </com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputLayout>

                <!-- ============================ Summary and save ============================
                     Two lines: what is about to be saved, and the position it will carry — the exact
                     coordinates once there is a fix, and "waiting for a GPS fix" until there is. The
                     second line is the screen's honesty about itself, shown before the user commits.

                     accessibilityLiveRegion polite: it changes as the form is filled in, and a screen
                     reader should mention the change without interrupting what is being typed. -->
                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/summaryText"
                    style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.Summary"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/spacing_lg"
                    android:accessibilityLiveRegion="polite"
                    tools:text="Untitled place — Vet\nWaiting for a GPS fix" />

                <!-- Disabled until the place has both a name and a fix. Disabled here means a solid
                     resting slab with pale ink, not a faded button — see attrs.xml,
                     colorDisabledContainer — and the label says which of the two is missing. -->
                <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
                    android:id="@+id/savePlaceButton"
                    style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.SaveButton"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/spacing_md"
                    tools:text="@string/add_place_save" />

            </LinearLayout>

        </androidx.core.widget.NestedScrollView>

    </LinearLayout>

</androidx.coordinatorlayout.widget.CoordinatorLayout>
